{"parentUuid":"8a986950-61eb-4898-ac30-37dbe26d4d5b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a122781128a284455","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14849487 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"96126d8a-6384-45af-a2fd-602ff1b3d40a","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:41:43.611Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14849487 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a122781128a284455","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-ab095323a3b740c00"}
{"parentUuid":"96126d8a-6384-45af-a2fd-602ff1b3d40a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a122781128a284455","attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01HYcRPVMCzuTiJGdgCwUSSA","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"599dbb0d-faa9-4f35-9c67-7e0af62fe152","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:41:51.225Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-a122781128a284455","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-ab095323a3b740c00"}
{"parentUuid":"599dbb0d-faa9-4f35-9c67-7e0af62fe152","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a122781128a284455","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CffscaedeKdJJk1f2JYdn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #134 for noninteractive-run/codex is merged. CI was all green, and `sr-checks` printed no refusals on the final run. The session-fork agent can rebase on it now.\n\n**What the judge flagged:** the git-repo-required check was never enforced or tested, and `--output-schema` was accepted but nothing recorded what it does.\n\n**Recordings captured (three new runs):**\n- **`noninteractive-run-git-check-refused`:** outside a git repository, without `--skip-git-repo-check` and without the sandbox bypass, the real `codex exec` prints \"Not inside a trusted directory and --skip-git-repo-check was not specified.\" and exits 1. It streams nothing and starts no session.\n- **`noninteractive-run-no-git-check`:** the same setup but with `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`. Real codex does not check at all in that case and runs normally. I found this by trying it by hand. The run keeps the \"no-git-check\" name because the file-guards refuse renaming a captured run.\n- **`noninteractive-run-output-schema`:** the real final message is JSON conforming to the schema, and the stream is otherwise identical to a run without `--output-schema`.\n\n**Mock changes:**\n- **Git-repo check:** `checkRepo` in `codex-mock/exec.go` now refuses a run outside a git repository unless `--skip-git-repo-check` or the sandbox bypass is given. It prints the recorded message to stderr and exits 1. I first put it in a new file, but the module-coverage rule refused that, so it lives in `exec.go`.\n- **Hook-trust notices:** the mock printed the two hook-trust notices only when hooks were configured. The new no-hook recordings show them printed regardless, so I removed that condition (and the now-unused `hooks.Config.Any`), which touches `Run` in `run.go`.\n- **`--output-schema`:** it is still accepted and ignored. The mock has no model, so the final message is the script's own. I declared that as a modeled-surface deviation in the cell, along with the unmodeled trusted-directory-via-config case. I cited the three new runs and left the `statement` untouched.\n\n**`capture.sh` options:** `no-git`, `no-skip-git-check`, `no-sandbox-bypass` and `schema.json`, all flat under `setup/`.\n\n**Tests:** `codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/noninteractive_repo_schema_test.go` has four tests marked `sr:proves noninteractive-run/codex`. They replay the recordings and assert exit code, stdout, stderr, no session started, and stream shape. They also check that the recorded schema message conforms.\n\n**Not covered:** I did not record running in a subdirectory of a repository without the flag, so the tests only assert a run in the repository root."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":170,"cache_read_input_tokens":150374,"output_tokens":938,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":170},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":938,"cache_read_input_tokens":150374,"cache_creation_input_tokens":170,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":170,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CffscaMGtPV2ToGqCHUdq","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3f903a9a-c421-44ed-aed9-c4064de1f5f5","timestamp":"2026-10-03T19:41:51.225Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/w